35,2,1,talk,Midori,,I found the joint clinic collapsed because neither side owned the rota. The shared nursing round also lost a third of visits. We need clear ownership.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The call-back trial cut readmissions by a fifth, but the joint clinic failed due to unclear ownership. We need a model that actually sticks.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"Nine posts unfilled, agency costs rising. Yet midwifery has slack. We must match the program to available staff, not just need.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The allocation is down a quarter, and home visits earn zero tariff. We can’t fund a program that generates no revenue.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, the rooms are full by mid-morning, and the shuttle misses most villages. If we can’t get patients here, no tariff matters.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
